Version 3.51e:
- bugfixes (total 9);
- minor changes (total 20);
- for team games with Explore Map, VPA now writes the combined map (obtained
  by merging XYPLANx.DAT maps of all team members) to a single XYPLAN.DAT file
  in the game directory, to be used by other VGAP utilities (idea: J.Shepherd);
- mine field info screen now shows how many torpedoes of each type can be
  scooped from the field, or how many it might have taken to create the field.

Version 3.51d:
- bugfixes (total 1);
- minor changes (total 3);

Version 3.51c:
- minor changes (total 2);

Version 3.51b:
- bugfixes (total 2);
- minor changes (total 4);

Version 3.51a:
- bugfixes (total 2);
- minor changes (total 16);
- map redrawing procedure has been sped up;
- VPA now accepts up to 11 player passwords from the command line ("/PW" key);
- Dynamic Map support added! VPA now stores the starmap in its database. The
  map may change from turn to turn, but VPA will always display it correctly;
- Explore Map support added! VPA now supports individual starmaps (XYPLANn.DAT),
  created by the EXPLMAP add-on;
- new MAP.INI option: Explore=Yes/No (default is No). When this option is
  enabled, VPA will use XYPLANn.DAT files rather than the main XYPLAN.DAT;
- default value for "KeepWayPoints" setting in VPA.INI is changed to "Off";
- new VPA.INI option: SmallFont=On/Off ([Interface] section, default is On).
  When this option is enabled, VPA displays planet names and marker labels on
  the map using built-in small nice font. However, on slow machines it may
  cause substantial slowdown in screen redraw procedure, so you can turn it
  Off to make VPA draw the map faster;
- new VPA.INI option: DullMissions=On/Off ([Interface] section, default is Off).
  When this option is enabled, the ship mission menu displays all possible
  missions, including ones that are normally useless, like Lay Mines for a
  freighter. Some add-ons might use these missions somehow;
- new VPA.INI option: DullMessages=On/Off ([Interface] section, default is Off).
  When this option is enabled, the message editor allows sending messages to
  all races, including dead and unplayed, with zero score. Normally messages
  to dead races can slow down Host operations, but PHOST and some add-ons can
  wipe all scores on purpose, to hide the information on ship numbers, etc.;
- new VPADATn.INI option: AcceptData0=Yes/No (default is No). This option
  controls whether VPA will accept data transmission messages from unknown
  senders or not;
- report files are written into the game directory, not current directory
  (from where you start VPA);
- in the report: when a planet has resources to build a starbase, the "Base"
  field in the "Planets" section contains a dot (idea: J.Schafer);
- new hot key: Ctrl-Alt-X - exit without saving changes. I don't know why would
  anybody need it, when UNDO is here, but still someone needs it.


Version 3.51:
- minor changes and bugfixes (total 65);
- M.O.T. interface has been changed. Now you don't have to press Enter to
  input a numeric value. Just type it in. When you press a digit key, VPA
  will automatically activate the input routine. Press Enter to finish the
  numeric input. Press Enter again when you want to leave M.O.T. session;
- VPA now can store and later retrieve up to 10 player-defined map positions.
  To store current map position, press Shift-Alt-<n>, where <n> is a numeric
  key "0".."9". Later you can go directly to that position by pressing Alt-<n>
  key. These map "bookmarks" are saved by VPA on exit and can be retrieved
  during subsequent VPA sessions (idea: A.Babanov);
- Center Map function is re-assigned to the "Z" key;
- new VPA.INI option: BadVideoOrMouse=Yes/No ([System] section, default is No).
  Some faulty video cards reportedly have problems with standard VGA video
  mode switching. Also, some buggy mouse drivers don't provide correct support
  for the standard 640x480 VGA video mode. If your screen goes blank or mouse
  pointer disappears upon exit from the construction yard or combat simulator
  screen, try setting BadVideoOrMouse=Yes. Although, in case of a bad mouse
  driver it's better just to change the driver;
- new VPA.INI option: LargePlanets=On/Off ([Interface] section, default is On).
  Determines whether or not VPA should draw enlarged planet circles in zoom
  map modes;
- in VPA combat simulator: now it's possible to repeat the previous battles.
  Press Shift-S instead of "S" key to go backwards through the sequence of
  possible battles between the given pair of combatants;
- VPA is now aware of Host 3.22.005 advanced cloakers (Resolute, Dark Wing);
- UNDO FEATURE IS HERE! Now you can scrap mines, factories and defense posts
  built during the current turn. Use Left arrow key (alone or with Ctrl, Alt
  or Shift) to scrap planetary structures via the M.O.T. interface (press "M",
  "A" or "D" key to enter the Structure Build mode);
- undo feature in supply selling;
- undo feature in base defense increment;
- undo feature in torpedo/fighter building;
- undo feature in tech level upgrading. Note: if you upgraded base tech level
  and later built ship parts or torpedoes of the respective tech, you may not
  downgrade the base tech level until you scrap all these parts or torpedoes;
- undo feature in shipbuilding. When you cancel shipbuilding orders, VPA
  automatically scraps ship parts built on the current turn. Using the "Minus"
  key, you can scrap ship parts built with the "Plus" key;
- undo feature in starbase construction (press "B" again to cancel the base);
- ship's fly path and trace can be drawn in different colors now. New "FlyPath"
  parameter has been added to VPA.INI color section;
- if a ship is being towed, its path under tow is shown on the screen. New
  "TowPath" parameter has been added to VPA.INI color section;
- if a ship is going to travel through a Firecloud Chunnel, the Chunnel path
  is shown on the screen using the "TowPath" color;
- old planet data in the planet info screen (from "N turns ago") is shown in
  a dark color now (idea: A.Shafir);
- new "OldPlanetInfo" parameter has been added to VPA.INI color section;
- report generation is re-assigned to F4 key (was F2);
- you can now save all changes you made without leaving the program (F2 key);
- no more confirmation on exit. With the UNDO feature it's not necessary;
- VPA is more reliable now as it tries to save data changes when run-time
  errors occur;
- jettisoning colonists is now allowed (as in WinPlan);
- map labels are now written with a smaller font;
- planet names are shown on the map! (in 1:1 and stronger zoom modes);
- new option in VPA.INI ("Interface" section): PlanetNames = On/Off (default
  is "On") - if this option is disabled, VPA shows planet numbers rather than
  names;
- planet names/numbers on the map can be turned on/off with Shift-P key;
- new marker type: a line between two user-defined map locations. Two line
  styles are supported - solid and dashed;
- in team mode: duplicate e-mail messages received by different players
  (for instance, universal messages) are not displayed repeatedly any more;
- anonymous messages are now recognized as e-mail (template: M.P.Castro);
- added HULLFUNC.DAT support. If you have this file in the game directory,
  VPA will use it;
- if one-engine towing is disabled in HCONFIG, then VPA doesn't allow setting
  Tow mission for such ships (idea: S.Bezgin). Generally, impossible missions
  (like Lay Mines for a freighter) are not present in the mission menu now;
- in the score screen it's now possible to compare the current turn score not
  only with the previous turn, but with any turn in the game. Use Shift-+/-
  keys to move in time the point of comparison (idea: F.Poiker);
- added a feature for supply selling during planet-to-ship cargo transfer.
  After all credits from the planet are loaded onto the ship, all further
  money loading commands will automatically sell supplies from the planet and
  load them as credits onto the ship. For example, you can press Shift-Left to
  load all credits, then Shift-Left once again to sell and load all supplies;
- in the Distance Mode with a locked ship you can double click on or near an
  object on the map to set the ship's waypoint to that object's location. E.g.,
  double click here is the same as click + Ctrl-click (idea: K.Tchernov);
- when you set waypoint for a ship that has warp=0, its warp factor is
  automatically set to match the engine tech level (idea: K.Tchernov);
- in the Distance Mode you can now change the ship's warp by pressing numeric
  keys ("0".."9"). Therefore, it's now possible to calculate multi-turn fly
  routes with variable speed en route;
- in the Distance Mode you can now activate/deactivate cloaking device of a
  ship able to cloak by pressing "C" key. Therefore, it's now possible to
  calculate multi-turn fly routes with variable cloaking status en route
  (idea: Yu.Kozachenko);
- Team Message. When playing in a team game (with all team member RSTs UNPACKed
  into the same directory), you can now send a message to all your teammates.
  Race selection menu in the message editor will display an option for that,
  and a special header will be inserted automatically into the message;
- message to host. Race selection menu in the message editor now has an option
  for sending messages to game host. When Host program receives such a message,
  it stores it in a file named HOSTMESS.TXT;
- new WinPlan message compatibility added. VPA now can read and store new
  format WinPlan messages. However, because of WinPlan software limitations,
  VPA may not allow you to write long messages (to the bottom of the message
  window) sometimes, if WinPlan message file (MESS35n.DAT) is present in the
  game directory;
- for a bidirectional wormhole VPA now draws a dashed line on the map between
  the two ends (idea: S.Frey);
- new VPA.INI option: AutoUseGravity=Yes/No ([Interface] section, default is
  No). When this options is enabled, and planetary gravity is enabled in Host
  configuration, then whenever you set your ship's waypoint to a planet, VPA
  will automatically adjust the waypoint to the edge of the planetery gravity
  well (idea: C.L.Mates), unless the ship is travelling on warp 1;
- new VPA.INI option: KeepWayPoints=Yes/No ([Interface] section, default is
  Yes). When this option is enabled, at the start of each turn VPA will
  automatically restore waypoints for your ships that were set on the
  previous turn, except for ships that ran out of fuel, were towed or
  chunnelled. This feature uses planetary gravity, so if a ship had its
  waypoint set to the edge of planetary warp well, the waypoint will be
  cleared once the ship reaches the planet;
- improved Extended Mission interface. Extended Missions are now chosen from
  a separate menu, while the main mission selection menu now includes a special
  item called "Ext. Misn." that is displayed when there are any Extended
  Missions available. VPA now supports parameter names for Extended
  Missions and displays these names during the mission setting. However, in
  the ship info screen Extended Mission parameters are displayed under their
  standard names "I" and "T";
- VPA now displays beam sweeping rate and torpedo minelaying capacity in
  the starbase construction yard screen (idea: A.Perovic);
- added a feature for fast hyperjump circle drawing on the map (idea: S.Frey).
  Press Ctrl-H to draw three circles - 340, 350 and 360 LYs - around the
  current pointer location.
